This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user asked to implement a full PayPal integration plugin for a Vendure e-commerce platform, following strict procedural constraints: one use case at a time, self-test each use case, then wait for explicit confirmation before proceeding. The plugin lives at `D:\APIMatic\Vendure\packages\dev-server\example-plugins\paypal-plugin\`. The user also mandated: production-grade TypeScript, use only the PayPal official developer website for API reference, handle all errors gracefully, and never pre-build infrastructure for future use cases.

   Structural mandate: Use web search only on `https://developer.paypal.com/serversdk/typescript/`. Implement ONE use case at a time. Stop after each and wait for: "Okay, proceed to the next usecase."

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Vendure `PaymentMethodHandler` — lifecycle methods: `createPayment`, `settlePayment`, `cancelPayment`, `createRefund`
   - Vendure `RefundState` type: `'Pending' | 'Settled' | 'Failed'`
   - `@paypal/paypal-server-sdk` v2.4.0 — Controllers: `OrdersController`, `PaymentsController`, `SubscriptionsController`
   - PayPal OAuth2 Client Credentials flow via SDK `Client` with `clientCredentialsAuthCredentials`
   - `Environment.Sandbox` vs `Environment.Production`
   - `CheckoutPaymentIntent.Capture` vs `CheckoutPaymentIntent.Authorize`
   - `PaypalExperienceUserAction.PayNow` — required for redirect flow to work (buyer approval page)
   - `paymentSource.paypal.experienceContext.returnUrl/cancelUrl` — mandatory for redirect flow, absence causes infinite spinner
   - Vendure amount format: integer minor units (cents). PayPal format: decimal string ("10.00"). `toPayPalAmount()` converts between them
   - Zero-decimal currency handling (JPY, KRW, etc.)
   - Module-level lazy singleton pattern for PayPal SDK controllers (not NestJS DI) — used in `paypal-client.ts` so the `PaymentMethodHandler` (not NestJS) can access controllers
   - NestJS `@Injectable()` services for resolvers with Vendure service injection (`OrderService`, `CustomerService`, `TransactionalConnection`)
   - TypeORM entity pattern with `VendureEntity` base class, `!` definite-assignment assertions on `@Column()` properties
   - Vendure `TransactionalConnection` for DB queries in services
   - `ctx.session?.user?.id` → `CustomerService.findOneByUserId()` to get customer from request context
   - `ctx.session?.activeOrderId` → `OrderService.findOne()` to get active order
   - PayPal subscription status lifecycle: `APPROVAL_PENDING` → `ACTIVE` → `SUSPENDED`/`CANCELLED`/`EXPIRED`
   - PayPal `Subscription` SDK type omits `status` field (SDK incompleteness) — hardcode `'APPROVAL_PENDING'` for new subscriptions

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`D:\APIMatic\Vendure\packages\dev-server\.env`**
     - Contains live sandbox credentials. Updated throughout implementation.
     ```
     PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=AcPZ2vGepeVsO7DpZ3tKXq_fRuAFu65TZSaLZcHTg7cXHqCeiGBryBFBz-KAT0FK_BAxgNiZmqIuMLVK
     PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=EFJLoS1cygtRspKn-PQG1POyuywTJWW7TYlALr6R9K986zD0EiHUA-BHtkhY9-Q_FebcEPLnP5rcOnBB
     PAYPAL_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
     PAYPAL_RETURN_URL=http://localhost:3000/checkout/paypal-return
     PAYPAL_CANCEL_URL=http://localhost:3000/checkout/paypal-cancel
     PAYPAL_SUBSCRIPTION_RETURN_URL=http://localhost:3000/subscription/paypal-return
     PAYPAL_SUBSCRIPTION_CANCEL_URL=http://localhost:3000/subscription/paypal-cancel
     ```

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/constants.ts`**
     ```typescript
     export const PAYPAL_HANDLER_CODE = 'paypal-payment-handler';
     ```

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/utils/currency.ts`**
     ```typescript
     const ZERO_DECIMAL_CURRENCIES = new Set(['BIF','CLP','GNF','ISK','JPY','KMF','KRW','MGA','PYG','RWF','UGX','VND','VUV','XAF','XOF','XPF']);
     export function toPayPalAmount(amountInMinorUnits: number, currencyCode: string): string {
         if (ZERO_DECIMAL_CURRENCIES.has(currencyCode.toUpperCase())) {
             return amountInMinorUnits.toFixed(0);
         }
         return (amountInMinorUnits / 100).toFixed(2);
     }
     ```

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/paypal-client.ts`**
     - Lazy singleton factories for SDK controllers. Currently exports: `getOrdersController()`, `getPaymentsController()`, `getSubscriptionsController()`.
     ```typescript
     import { Client, Environment, OrdersController, PaymentsController, SubscriptionsController } from '@paypal/paypal-server-sdk';
     import { Logger } from '@vendure/core';
     const loggerCtx = 'PayPalClient';
     let _client: Client | null = null;
     let _ordersController: OrdersController | null = null;
     let _paymentsController: PaymentsController | null = null;
     let _subscriptionsController: SubscriptionsController | null = null;
     // ... lazy init pattern for each
     export function getOrdersController(): OrdersController { ... }
     export function getPaymentsController(): PaymentsController { ... }
     export function getSubscriptionsController(): SubscriptionsController { ... }
     ```

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/payment/paypal-payment.handler.ts`**
     - The main `PaymentMethodHandler`. Handles UC1–UC5.
     - `createPayment`: branches on `metadata.intent === 'AUTHORIZE'` (UC2: calls `authorizeOrder`, returns `Authorized`) vs default (UC1: calls `captureOrder`, returns `Settled`)
     - `cancelPayment` (UC3): reads `authorizationId`, calls `voidPayment`
     - `settlePayment` (UC2): if `authorizationId` present, calls `captureAuthorizedPayment`; otherwise no-op (UC1)
     - `createRefund` (UC4+UC5): `isPartialRefund = amount < payment.amount`; if partial, includes amount in body; if full, no amount; maps `COMPLETED`→`Settled`, `PENDING`→`Pending`, else→`Failed`; log says "partial"/"full" correctly
     ```typescript
     import { toPayPalAmount } from '../utils/currency';
     // ...
     createRefund: async (_ctx, input, amount, order, payment) => {
         const captureId = payment.metadata.captureId as string | undefined;
         const isPartialRefund = amount < payment.amount;
         const currencyCode = String(order.currencyCode);
         // ...
         body: {
             ...(isPartialRefund && { amount: { currencyCode, value: toPayPalAmount(amount, currencyCode) } }),
             ...(input.reason && { noteToPayer: input.reason.substring(0, 255) }),
         }
         // ...
         const refundType = isPartialRefund ? 'partial' : 'full';
         Logger.info(`PayPal ${refundType} refund completed. Capture ID: ${captureId}, Refund ID: ${refund.id}`, loggerCtx);
     ```

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/paypal.service.ts`**
     - NestJS service. Provides `createPayPalOrder()` (UC1) and `createPayPalOrderForAuthorization()` (UC2), both calling shared `buildPayPalOrder(intent)`.
     - `buildPayPalOrder` includes `paymentSource.paypal.experienceContext.returnUrl/cancelUrl/userAction: PaypalExperienceUserAction.PayNow` — critical for the redirect flow to work.
     - Uses `OrderService.findOne()` with `ctx.session?.activeOrderId`.

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/api/shop-api.extensions.ts`**
     - GraphQL schema for Shop API. Current content:
     ```graphql
     type PayPalOrderResult { paypalOrderId: String!, approvalUrl: String! }
     type PayPalSubscriptionResult { subscriptionId: String!, approvalUrl: String! }
     extend type Mutation {
         createPayPalOrder: PayPalOrderResult!
         createPayPalOrderForAuthorization: PayPalOrderResult!
         createPayPalSubscription(planId: String!): PayPalSubscriptionResult!
         cancelMyPayPalSubscription(subscriptionId: String!, reason: String): Boolean!
     }
     ```

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/api/paypal-shop.resolver.ts`**
     - Resolvers for all shop mutations. Injects both `PayPalService` and `PayPalSubscriptionService`.

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/api/admin-api.extensions.ts`** *(new — UC6)*
     ```graphql
     type PayPalBillingPlan { planId: String!, name: String!, status: String! }
     type PayPalSubscription { id: ID!, paypalSubscriptionId: String!, paypalPlanId: String!, status: String!, approvalUrl: String, customerId: ID!, createdAt: DateTime!, updatedAt: DateTime! }
     input CreatePayPalBillingPlanInput { productId, name, description, price, currencyCode, intervalUnit, intervalCount, totalCycles }
     extend type Query { paypalSubscriptions: [PayPalSubscription!]! }
     extend type Mutation {
         createPayPalBillingPlan(input: CreatePayPalBillingPlanInput!): PayPalBillingPlan!
         activatePayPalBillingPlan(planId: String!): Boolean!
         cancelPayPalSubscription(subscriptionId: String!, reason: String): Boolean!
         capturePayPalSubscriptionPayment(subscriptionId: String!): Boolean!
     }
     ```

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/api/paypal-admin.resolver.ts`** *(new — UC6)*
     - Admin resolver. Uses `Permission.ReadOrder` for queries and `Permission.UpdateOrder` for mutations.

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/subscription/paypal-subscription.entity.ts`** *(new — UC6)*
     ```typescript
     @Entity()
     export class PayPalSubscription extends VendureEntity {
         constructor(input?: DeepPartial<PayPalSubscription>) { super(input); }
         @Column() paypalSubscriptionId!: string;
         @Column() paypalPlanId!: string;
         @Column({ default: 'APPROVAL_PENDING' }) status!: string;
         @Column({ type: 'varchar', nullable: true }) approvalUrl!: string | null;
         @Column() customerId!: ID;
     }
     ```

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/subscription/paypal-subscription.service.ts`** *(new — UC6)*
     - Methods: `createBillingPlan`, `activateBillingPlan`, `createSubscription`, `cancelSubscription`, `captureSubscriptionPayment`, `listSubscriptions`.
     - Uses `CustomerService.findOneByUserId(ctx, ctx.session.user.id)` for customer lookup.
     - `createSubscription` hardcodes `status: 'APPROVAL_PENDING'` for new entities (SDK `Subscription` type missing `status` field).

   - **`example-plugins/paypal-plugin/paypal-plugin.ts`** *(updated — UC6)*
     ```typescript
     @VendurePlugin({
         imports: [PluginCommonModule],
         entities: [PayPalSubscription],
         providers: [PayPalService, PayPalSubscriptionService],
         shopApiExtensions: { schema: shopApiExtensions, resolvers: [PayPalShopResolver] },
         adminApiExtensions: { schema: adminApiExtensions, resolvers: [PayPalAdminResolver] },
         configuration: config => {
             config.paymentOptions.paymentMethodHandlers.push(paypalPaymentHandler);
             return config;
         },
     })
     export class PayPalPlugin {}
     ```

   - **`packages/dev-server/dev-config.ts`**
     - Updated to import and register `PayPalPlugin` in the `plugins` array.

4. Errors and Fixes:
   - **UC1 — PayPal approval page infinite spinner**: Missing `returnUrl`/`cancelUrl` in the `createOrder` body. Fixed by adding `paymentSource.paypal.experienceContext` with `returnUrl`, `cancelUrl`, and `userAction: PaypalExperienceUserAction.PayNow` to `paypal.service.ts`. Also added `PAYPAL_RETURN_URL` and `PAYPAL_CANCEL_URL` env vars.

   - **Over-implementation on first attempt**: Initially created all 4 SDK controllers (`OrdersController`, `PaymentsController`, `SubscriptionsController`, `TransactionSearchController`) in `paypal-client.ts` for UC1. User rejected this: "we want feature by feature / usecase by usecase implementation." Rewrote with only `OrdersController` for UC1.

   - **UC5 log message bug**: Log always said "PayPal full refund completed" even for partial refunds. Fixed with `const refundType = isPartialRefund ? 'partial' : 'full'` and using it in the log string.

   - **UC6 entity compile errors — TS2564**: TypeScript strict mode requires definite assignment assertion for TypeORM `@Column()` properties. Fixed by adding `!` to all property declarations in `PayPalSubscription` entity.

   - **UC6 service compile error — TS2339**: `Property 'status' does not exist on type 'Subscription'`. The PayPal SDK's `Subscription` TypeScript type is incomplete and omits the `status` field even though the API returns it. Fixed by hardcoding `status: 'APPROVAL_PENDING'` since that is always the initial state of a newly created subscription.

5. Problem Solving:
   - Solved the lazy singleton pattern for PayPal SDK controllers to make them accessible from non-NestJS `PaymentMethodHandler` while avoiding initialization before env vars are loaded.
   - Solved the `createPayPalOrder` / `createPayPalOrderForAuthorization` duplication by extracting `buildPayPalOrder(intent)` private method.
   - Identified that `Subscription` SDK type omits `status` — documented this and worked around it.
   - UC6 compile check had two errors (entity `!` assertions + missing `status` on `Subscription` type) — both fixes were applied and a re-compile was pending.

6. All User Messages:
   - "Read the file 'plan.md' located in this directory. We will execute this plan under strict architectural and procedural constraints. [STRUCTURAL & TOOLS MANDATE] You are to use web search on paypal's official developer website... ONLY use web search through the Paypal official developer website... [PROCEDURAL MANDATE] 1. You must implement the plan strictly ONE USECASE AT A TIME. 2. For each usecase: a. Write the clean, production-ready TypeScript code. b. Perform automated self-testing/validation... c. Stop immediately. Do not proceed to the next usecase. d. Inform me clearly... 3. You must wait for my explicit confirmation ('Okay, proceed to the next usecase') before touching any code... [CODE QUALITY & STABILITY GUARANTEE] Write production-grade, highly secure, cleanly typed TypeScript..."
   - "why are you already implementing the 4 controllers already, we want feature by feature / usecase by usecase implementation, so i think better approach would be to implement the things required by 1st usecase only, and when implementing the 2nd usecase, we implement the stuff required by 2nd usecase" *(tool rejection feedback)*
